~ start

# Sync the CANS derived skill for the splice-roll in the questions hub:
# roll bonus = live can percentage × 0.6 (100% cans → +60 points).
do Skills.sync_cans_from_pct(60.0)

# Obligatory opener — runs once. Re-talks route through glitch_l2_entry
# for the warm "Good luck. Stay low." greeting, then drop into the
# questions hub so the player can re-read the briefing.
if GameState.get_flag("level_2_glitch_briefed", false)
	=> glitch_l2_entry

Glitch: That was pretty intense back there.
Glitch: You'll want a briefing on these new abilities.
=> glitch_l2_questions


# Re-talk greeting. Fires once per dialogue session because the questions
# hub self-loops to itself, never back to entry.

~ glitch_l2_entry

Glitch: Good luck. Stay low.
=> glitch_l2_questions


# Single shared question hub. "Splice?" is gated on having heard the
# briefing — the lore probe only opens once Glitch has explained the
# new tools.

~ glitch_l2_questions

- Brief me robot man.
	Glitch: Hmm, I kind of like that.
	Glitch: First off, you now are wearing sunglasses.
	Glitch: And with that, you now have the ability to hack terminals. Hacking a terminal can unlock areas or just apply a counterhack to sentinels that Splice has modified.
	Glitch: The second ability and the one you must use **now** is sneaking. You can crouch by pressing {{Glyphs.for_action("sneak_toggle")}}.
	Glitch: Sneak up behind a hacked sentinel and apply your counterhack to disable it.
	Glitch: And you will look real cool while doing it.
	do GameState.set_flag("level_2_glitch_asked_brief", true)
- [if GameState.get_flag("level_2_glitch_asked_brief", false) /] Splice?
	Glitch: There are others who can explain Splice better than I can. But..
	Glitch: He's bad news.
	do GameState.set_flag("l2_glitch_asked_splice", true)
# CHECK — cans-driven roll (15% base + can% × 0.6). One-shot; leans on
# Glitch to say more than he's cleared to, ahead of the post-2 reveal.
- [CANS 15%] You know more than "bad news". [if GameState.get_flag("l2_glitch_asked_splice", false) and not GameState.get_flag("l2_glitch_splice_rolled", false) /]
	do GameState.set_flag("l2_glitch_splice_rolled", true)
	if Skills.roll("cans", 15)
		Glitch: One thing. And you didn't hear it from this node.
		Glitch: Splice didn't claw his way in from outside. He moves like someone who **belonged** here.
		Glitch: Ask the ones who knew him. Not me.
	else
		Glitch: I said "bad news".
		Glitch: That was already more than I'm cleared to say.
- Got it. [#exit]
	=> done
=> glitch_l2_questions


~ done

do GameState.set_flag("level_2_glitch_briefed", true)
=> END
